  "conclusion": "The null hypothesis was not rejected. Within this SCOTUS corpus, matched prosodic features did not improve register classification beyond text. Prosody-only models were weak, real prosody did not meaningfully beat a shuffled-prosody placebo, and adding prosody to the text stacker caused six regressions and zero fixes.",
